     matches: true,\n      addEventListener: addEventListenerMock,\n      removeEventListener: removeEventListenerMock,\n    });\n\n    const { result } = renderHook(() => useIsMobile());\n    expect(result.current).toBe(true); // < 768 = mobile\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. `src/hooks/use-socket.ts`\n\n### Untested Functions\n- ✗ Socket initialization\n- ✗ Event handlers (connect, disconnect, state_push, chef_status)\n- ✗ `subscribe` function\n- ✗ CSRF integration\n- ✗ Cleanup on unmount\n\n### Missing Edge Cases\n- Socket connection failures\n- Malformed state_push data\n- Missing snapshot in envelope\n- CSRF token failures\n- Rapid subscribe calls\n- Connect/disconnect cycles\n\n### Test Skeletons\n\n```typescript\n// __tests__/hooks/use-socket.test.ts\nimport { renderHook, act } from '@testing-library/react';\nimport { useSocket } from '@/hooks/use-socket';\nimport * as socketClient from '@/lib/socket-client';\nimport * as csrfModule from '@/lib/csrf';\nimport { EventEmitter } from 'events';\n\njest.mock('@/lib/socket-client');\njest.mock('@/lib/csrf');\n\nclass MockSocket extends EventEmitter {\n  connected = false;\n  connect = jest.fn(() => { this.connected = true; });\n  disconnect = jest.fn(() => { this.connected = false; });\n  emit = jest.fn();\n  off = jest.fn();\n}\n\ndescribe('useSocket', () => {\n  let mockSocket: MockSocket;\n\n  beforeEach(() => {\n    mockSocket = new MockSocket();\n    (socketClient.initStateSyncSocket as jest.Mock).mockReturnValue(mockSocket);\n    (socketClient.getStateSyncSocket as jest.Mock).mockReturnValue(mockSocket);\n    (csrfModule.getCsrfToken as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue('test-token');\n  });\n\n  afterEach(() => {\n    jest.clearAllMocks();\n  });\n\n  it('should initialize socket on mount', () => {\n    renderHook(() => useSocket());\n    expect(socketClient.initStateSyncSocket).toHaveBeenCalled();\n  });\n\n  it('should set connected to true on connect event', () => {\n    const { result } = renderHook(() => useSocket());\n    \n    act(() => {\n      mockSocket.emit('connect');\n    });\n    \n    expect(result.current.connected).toBe(true);\n  });\n\n  it('should emit state_request on connect', () => {\n    renderHook(() => useSocket());\n    \n    act(() => {\n      mockSocket.emit('connect');\n    });\n    \n    expect(mockSocket.emit).toHaveBeenCalledWith(\n      'state_request',\n      expect.objectContaining({\n        context: null,\n        log_from: 0,\n        notifications_from: 0,\n      })\n    );\n  });\n\n  it('should update snapshot on state_push event', () => {\n    const { result } = renderHook(() => useSocket());\n    \n    const mockSnapshot = {\n      context: 'ctx-1',\n      logs: [{ no: 1, id: 'log-1', type: 'response', content: 'Test', timestamp: 1000 }],\n      log_progress_active: false,\n    };\n    \n    act(() => {\n      mockSocket.emit('state_push', {\n        data: { snapshot: mockSnapshot },\n      });\n    });\n    \n    expect(result.current.snapshot).toMatchObject(mockSnapshot);\n  });\n\n  it('should handle state_push with missing snapshot', () => {\n    const { result } = renderHook(() => useSocket());\n    const consoleSpy = jest.spyOn(console, 'warn').mockImplementation();\n    \n    act(() => {\n      mockSocket.emit('state_push', { data: {} });\n    });\n    \n    expect(consoleSpy).toHaveBeenCalledWith(\n      expect.stringContaining('no snapshot'),\n      expect.anything()\n    );\n    expect(result.current.snapshot).toBeNull();\n    \n    consoleSpy.mockRestore();\n  });\n\n  it('should update chefStatus on chef_status event', () => {\n    const { result } = renderHook(() => useSocket());\n    \n    const mockStatus = {\n      status: 'working' as const,\n      text: 'Processing order',\n      active: true,\n    };\n    \n    act(() => {\n      mockSocket.emit('chef_status', mockStatus);\n    });\n    \n    expect(result.current.chefStatus).toEqual(mockStatus);\n  });\n\n  it('should subscribe to context', () => {\n    const { result } = renderHook(() => useSocket());\n    mockSocket.connected = true;\n    \n    act(() => {\n      result.current.subscribe('ctx-123');\n    });\n    \n    expect(mockSocket.emit).toHaveBeenCalledWith(\n      'state_request',\n      expect.objectContaining({\n        context: 'ctx-123',\n        log_from: 0,\n      })\n    );\n  });\n\n  it('should not subscribe when socket is disconnected', () => {\n    const { result } = renderHook(() => useSocket());\n    mockSocket.connected = false;\n    \n    act(() => {\n      result.current.subscribe('ctx-123');\n    });\n    \n    // Should not emit if not connected\n    const emitCalls = (mockSocket.emit as jest.Mock).mock.calls.filter(\n      ([event]) => event === 'state_request'\n    );\n    expect(emitCalls.length).toBe(0);\n  });\n\n  it('should disconnect socket on unmount', () => {\n    const { unmount } = renderHook(() => useSocket());\n    \n    unmount();\n    \n    expect(mockSocket.disconnect).toHaveBeenCalled();\n    expect(mockSocket.off).toHaveBeenCalledWith('connect');\n    expect(mockSocket.off).toHaveBeenCalledWith('disconnect');\n    expect(mockSocket.off).toHaveBeenCalledWith('state_push');\n    expect(mockSocket.off).toHaveBeenCalledWith('chef_status');\n  });\n\n  it('should handle CSRF token failure gracefully', async () => {\n    (csrfModule.getCsrfToken as jest.Mock).mockRejectedValue(new Error('CSRF failed'));\n    \n    renderHook(() => useSocket());\n    \n    // Should still attempt to connect even if CSRF fails\n    await act(async () => {\n      await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 0));\n    });\n    \n    expect(mockSocket.connect).toHaveBeenCalled();\n  });\n\n  it('should track logFromRef and increment on state_push', () => {\n    const { result } = renderHook(() => useSocket());\n    \n    const snapshot1 = {\n      logs: [{ no: 5, id: 'log-5', type: 'response', content: 'Test', timestamp: 1000 }],\n      log_progress_active: false,\n    };\n    \n    act(() => {\n      mockSocket.emit('state_push', { data: { snapshot: snapshot1 } });\n    });\n    \n    // Next subscribe should use log_from = 6 (last log.no + 1)\n    mockSocket.connected = true;\n    act(() => {\n      result.current.subscribe('ctx-new');\n    });\n    \n    // Note: logFromRef is internal, but we can verify by checking the emit call\n    // In a real implementation, this would be reset to 0 on subscribe\n    expect(mockSocket.emit).toHaveBeenCalledWith(\n      'state_request',\n      expect.objectContaining({\n        log_from: 0, // Reset on subscribe\n      })\n    );\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. `src/hooks/use-workspace.ts`\n\n### Untested Functions\n- ✗ Data fetching logic\n- ✗ `refresh` function\n- ✗ Error handling\n- ✗ Response normalization (array vs object)\n\n### Missing Edge Cases\n- Network failures\n- Non-200 responses\n- Malformed JSON\n- Concurrent refreshes\n- Endpoint with existing query params\n\n### Test Skeletons\n\n```typescript\n// __tests__/hooks/use-workspace.test.ts\nimport { renderHook, waitFor, act } from '@testing-library/react';\nimport { useWorkspace } from '@/hooks/use-workspace';\n\nglobal.fetch = jest.fn();\n\ndescribe('useWorkspace', () => {\n  beforeEach(() => {\n    jest.clearAllMocks();\n  });\n\n  it('should fetch data on mount', async () => {\n    const mockData = [{ id: 1, name: 'Item 1' }];\n    (global.fetch as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue({\n      ok: true,\n      json: async () => mockData,\n    });\n\n    const { result } = renderHook(() => useWorkspace('/api/items'));\n\n    expect(result.current.loading).toBe(true);\n\n    await waitFor(() => {\n      expect(result.current.loading).toBe(false);\n    });\n\n    expect(result.current.data).toEqual(mockData);\n    expect(result.current.error).toBeNull();\n  });\n\n  it('should append locationId to URL if provided', async () => {\n    (global.fetch as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue({\n      ok: true,\n      json: async () => [],\n    });\n\n    renderHook(() => useWorkspace('/api/items', 'loc-123'));\n\n    await waitFor(() => {\n      expect(global.fetch).toHaveBeenCalledWith(\n        '/api/items?location_id=loc-123',\n        expect.objectContaining({ credentials: 'include' })\n      );\n    });\n  });\n\n  it('should normalize response objects with items/data field', async () => {\n    const mockResponse = {\n      items: [{ id: 1 }, { id: 2 }],\n      total: 2,\n    };\n    \n    (global.fetch as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue({\n      ok: true,\n      json: async () => mockResponse,\n    });\n\n    const { result } = renderHook(() => useWorkspace('/api/items'));\n\n    await waitFor(() => {\n      expect(result.current.data).toEqual(mockResponse.items);\n    });\n  });\n\n  it('should handle fetch errors', async () => {\n    (global.fetch as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue({\n      ok: false,\n      status: 500,\n    });\n\n    const { result } = renderHook(() => useWorkspace('/api/items'));\n\n    await waitFor(() => {\n      expect(result.current.error).toBe('500');\n      expect(result.current.data).toEqual([]);\n      expect(result.current.loading).toBe(false);\n    });\n  });\n\n  it('should handle network errors', async () => {\n    (global.fetch as jest.Mock).mockRejectedValue(new Error('Network error'));\n\n    const { result } = renderHook(() => useWorkspace('/api/items'));\n\n    await waitFor(() => {\n      expect(result.current.error).toBe('Network error');\n      expect(result.current.data).toEqual([]);\n    });\n  });\n\n  it('should refetch data when refresh is called', async () => {\n    (global.fetch as jest.Mock)\n      .mockResolvedValueOnce({\n        ok: true,\n        json: async () => [{ id: 1 }],\n      })\n      .mockResolvedValueOnce({\n        ok: true,\n        json: async () => [{ id: 2 }],\n      });\n\n    const { result } = renderHook(() => useWorkspace('/api/items'));\n\n    await waitFor(() => {\n      expect(result.current.data).toEqual([{ id: 1 }]);\n    });\n\n    act(() => {\n      result.current.refresh();\n    });\n\n    await waitFor(() => {\n      expect(result.current.data).toEqual([{ id: 2 }]);\n    });\n\n    expect(global.fetch).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(2);\n  });\n\n  it('should handle malformed JSON responses', async () => {\n    (global.fetch as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue({\n      ok: true,\n      json: async () => { throw new Error('Invalid JSON'); },\n    });\n\n    const { result } = renderHook(() => useWorkspace('/api/items'));\n\n    await waitFor(() => {\n      expect(result.current.error).toBeTruthy();\n      expect(result.current.data).toEqual([]);\n    });\n  });\n\n  it('should handle concurrent refresh calls', async () => {\n    (global.fetch as jest.Mock).mockImplementation(() =>\n      new Promise(resolve => \n        setTimeout(() => resolve({ ok: true, json: async () => [] }), 50)\n      )\n    );\n\n    const { result } = renderHook(() => useWorkspace('/api/items'));\n\n    act(() => {\n      result.current.refresh();\n      result.current.refresh();\n      result.current.refresh();\n    });\n\n    await waitFor(() => {\n      expect(result.current.loading).toBe(false);\n    });\n\n    // Should have called fetch for initial + 3 refreshes = 4 times\n    expect(global.fetch).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(4);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. `src/lib/csrf.ts`\n\n### Untested Functions\n- ✗ `getCsrfToken` with caching\n- ✗ `getCsrfToken` concurrent calls\n- ✗ `getRuntimeId`\n- ✗ `clearCsrfToken`\n- ✗ Cookie setting logic\n\n### Missing Edge Cases\n- Concurrent getCsrfToken calls (promise caching)\n- Fetch failures\n- Response with `ok: false`\n- Missing token/runtime_id in response\n- Cookie format validation\n\n### Test Skeletons\n\n```typescript\n// __tests__/lib/csrf.test.ts\nimport { getCsrfToken, getRuntimeId, clearCsrfToken } from '@/lib/csrf';\n\nglobal.fetch = jest.fn();\n\ndescribe('csrf', () => {\n  beforeEach(() => {\n    jest.clearAllMocks();\n    clearCsrfToken(); // Reset state\n    Object.defineProperty(document, 'cookie', {\n      writable: true,\n      value: '',\n    });\n  });\n\n  describe('getCsrfToken', () => {\n    it('should fetch and cache CSRF token', async () => {\n      (global.fetch as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue({\n        json: async () => ({ ok: true, token: 'test-token', runtime_id: 'runtime-123' }),\n      });\n\n      const token = await getCsrfToken();\n\n      expect(token).toBe('test-token');\n      expect(global.fetch).toHaveBeenCalledWith('/csrf_token', { credentials: 'include' });\n    });\n\n    it('should return cached token on subsequent calls', async () => {\n      (global.fetch as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue({\n        json: async () => ({ ok: true, token: 'cached-token', runtime_id: 'runtime-123' }),\n      });\n\n      const token1 = await getCsrfToken();\n      const token2 = await getCsrfToken();\n\n      expect(token1).toBe('cached-token');\n      expect(token2).toBe('cached-token');\n      expect(global.fetch).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1); // Only fetched once\n    });\n\n    it('should handle concurrent calls with promise caching', async () => {\n      (global.fetch as jest.Mock).mockImplementation(() =>\n        new Promise(resolve =>\n          setTimeout(() => resolve({ json: async () => ({ ok: true, token: 'concurrent-token', runtime_id: 'runtime-123' }) }), 50)\n        )\n      );\n\n      const [token1, token2, token3] = await Promise.all([\n        getCsrfToken(),\n        getCsrfToken(),\n        getCsrfToken(),\n      ]);\n\n      expect(token1).toBe('concurrent-token');\n      expect(token2).toBe('concurrent-token');\n      expect(token3).toBe('concurrent-token');\n      expect(global.fetch).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1); // Only one fetch\n    });\n\n    it('should throw error when response ok is false', async () => {\n      (global.fetch as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue({\n        json: async () => ({ ok: false, error: 'Invalid request' }),\n      });\n\n      await expect(getCsrfToken()).rejects.toThrow('Invalid request');\n    });\n\n    it('should throw error when token is missing', async () => {\n      (global.fetch as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue({\n        json: async () => ({ ok: true, runtime_id: 'runtime-123' }), // No token\n      });\n\n      await expect(getCsrfToken()).rejects.toThrow('Failed to get CSRF token');\n    });\n\n    it('should set cookie with correct format', async () => {\n      const setCookieSpy = jest.spyOn(document, 'cookie', 'set');\n      \n      (global.fetch as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue({\n        json: async () => ({ ok: true, token: 'cookie-token', runtime_id: 'runtime-456' }),\n      });\n\n      await getCsrfToken();\n\n      expect(document.cookie).toContain('csrf_token_runtime-456=cookie-token');\n      expect(document.cookie).toContain('SameSite=Strict');\n      expect(document.cookie).toContain('Path=/');\n    });\n\n    it('should handle network errors', async () => {\n      (global.fetch as jest.Mock).mockRejectedValue(new Error('Network failure'));\n\n      await expect(getCsrfToken()).rejects.toThrow('Network failure');\n    });\n  });\n\n  describe('getRuntimeId', () => {\n    it('should return null initially', () => {\n      expect(getRuntimeId()).toBeNull();\n    });\n\n    it('should return runtime ID after getCsrfToken', async () => {\n      (global.fetch as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue({\n        json: async () => ({ ok: true, token: 'token', runtime_id: 'runtime-789' }),\n      });\n\n      await getCsrfToken();\n\n      expect(getRuntimeId()).toBe('runtime-789');\n    });\n  });\n\n  describe('clearCsrfToken', () => {\n    it('should clear cached token and runtime ID', async () => {\n      (global.fetch as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue({\n        json: async () => ({ ok: true, token: 'clear-token', runtime_id: 'runtime-clear' }),\n      });\n\n      await getCsrfToken();\n      expect(getRuntimeId()).toBe('runtime-clear');\n\n      clearCsrfToken();\n\n      expect(getRuntimeId()).toBeNull();\n\n      // Should fetch again after clearing\n      (global.fetch as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue({\n        json: async () => ({ ok: true, token: 'new-token', runtime_id: 'runtime-new' }),\n      });\n\n      await getCsrfToken();\n      expect(global.fetch).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(2);\n    });\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## 8. `src/lib/expo-messages.ts`\n\n### Untested Functions\n- ✗ `getExpoMessage` for all log types\n- ✗ `getCompletionMessage`\n- ✗ Randomization logic\n\n### Missing Edge Cases\n- Unknown tool names\n- Missing/null heading\n- Empty log types\n- Randomization distribution\n\n### Test Skeletons\n\n```typescript\n// __tests__/lib/expo-messages.test.ts\nimport { getExpoMessage, getCompletionMessage } from '@/lib/expo-messages';\nimport type { A0LogEntry } from '@/lib/types';\n\ndescribe('expo-messages', () => {\n  describe('getExpoMessage', () => {\n    it('should return tool-specific message for known tools', () => {\n      const log: A0LogEntry = {\n        no: 1,\n        id: 'log-1',\n        type: 'tool',\n        heading: 'Using food_cost_tool...',\n        content: '',\n        kvps: {},\n        timestamp: 1000,\n        agentno: 0,\n      };\n\n      const message = getExpoMessage(log);\n\n      expect(message).toBeTruthy();\n      expect(message).toMatch(/food|cost|produce|avocado/i);\n    });\n\n    it('should return default message for unknown tools', () => {\n      const log: A0LogEntry = {\n        no: 1,\n        id: 'log-1',\n        type: 'tool',\n        heading: 'Using unknown_tool...',\n        content: '',\n        kvps: {},\n        timestamp: 1000,\n        agentno: 0,\n      };\n\n      const message = getExpoMessage(log);\n\n      expect(message).toBeTruthy();\n      expect(['Working on it...', 'One moment...', 'On it, Chef...']).toContain(message);\n    });\n\n    it('should return agent delegation message for agent logs', () => {\n      const log: A0LogEntry = {\n        no: 1,\n        id: 'log-1',\n        type: 'agent',\n        heading: 'Food Cost Analyst',\n        content: '',\n        kvps: {},\n        timestamp: 1000,\n        agentno: 1,\n      };\n\n      const message = getExpoMessage(log);\n\n      expect(message).toBe('Delegating to Food Cost Analyst...');\n    });\n\n    it('should return delegation message for subagent logs', () => {\n      const log: A0LogEntry = {\n        no: 1,\n        id: 'log-1',\n        type: 'subagent',\n        heading: 'Inventory Checker',\n        content: '',\n        kvps: {},\n        timestamp: 1000,\n        agentno: 2,\n      };\n\n      const message = getExpoMessage(log);\n\n      expect(message).toBe('Delegating to Inventory Checker...');\n    });\n\n    it('should return content for progress logs', () => {\n      const log: A0LogEntry = {\n        no: 1,\n        id: 'log-1',\n        type: 'progress',\n        heading: '',\n        content: 'Processing invoice 3 of 10...',\n        kvps: {},\n        timestamp: 1000,\n        agentno: 0,\n      };\n\n      const message = getExpoMessage(log);\n\n      expect(message).toBe('Processing invoice 3 of 10...');\n    });\n\n    it('should return null for non-relevant log types', () => {\n      const log: A0LogEntry = {\n        no: 1,\n        id: 'log-1',\n        type: 'user',\n        heading: '',\n        content: 'User message',\n        kvps: {},\n        timestamp: 1000,\n        agentno: 0,\n      };\n\n      const message = getExpoMessage(log);\n\n      expect(message).toBeNull();\n    });\n\n    it('should handle missing heading gracefully', () => {\n      const log: A0LogEntry = {\n        no: 1,\n        id: 'log-1',\n        type: 'agent',\n        heading: '',\n        content: '',\n        kvps: {},\n        timestamp: 1000,\n        agentno: 1,\n      };\n\n      const message = getExpoMessage(log);\n\n      expect(message).toBe('Delegating to a specialist...');\n    });\n\n    it('should handle null log gracefully', () => {\n      const message = getExpoMessage(null as any);\n      expect(message).toBeNull();\n    });\n  });\n\n  describe('getCompletionMessage', () => {\n    it('should return one of the completion messages', () => {\n      const message = getCompletionMessage();\n\n      expect(['Heard.', 'Service.', 'All set.', 'Done, Chef.']).toContain(message);\n    });\n\n    it('should randomize completion messages', () => {\n      const messages = new Set<string>();\n      \n      for (let i = 0; i < 50; i++) {\n        messages.add(getCompletionMessage());\n      }\n\n      // With 50 calls, we should see at least 2 different messages\n      expect(messages.size).toBeGreaterThan(1);\n    });\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## 9. `src/lib/socket-client.ts`\n\n### Untested Functions\n- ✗ `initStateSyncSocket`\n- ✗ `getStateSyncSocket`\n- ✗ `disconnectAll`\n- ✗ Auth callback logic\n- ✗ CSRF error handling in auth\n- ✗ connect_error event handler\n\n### Missing Edge Cases\n- Multiple initStateSyncSocket calls\n- Auth callback promise rejection\n- CSRF token fetch failure\n- Socket already connected\n- Disconnect while connecting\n\n### Test Skeletons\n\n```typescript\n// __tests__/lib/socket-client.test.ts\nimport { initStateSyncSocket, getStateSyncSocket, disconnectAll } from '@/lib/socket-client';\nimport { io } from 'socket.io-client';\nimport * as csrfModule from '@/lib/csrf';\n\njest.mock('socket.io-client');\njest.mock('@/lib/csrf');\n\ndescribe('socket-client', () => {\n  let mockSocket: any;\n\n  beforeEach(() => {\n    jest.clearAllMocks();\n    \n    mockSocket = {\n      on: jest.fn(),\n      off: jest.fn(),\n      disconnect: jest.fn(),\n      connected: false,\n    };\n\n    (io as jest.Mock).mockReturnValue(mockSocket);\n    (csrfModule.getCsrfToken as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue('test-token');\n    (csrfModule.clearCsrfToken as jest.Mock).mockImplementation(() => {});\n  });\n\n  describe('initStateSyncSocket', () => {\n    it('should create socket with correct config', () => {\n      initStateSyncSocket();\n\n      expect(io).toHaveBeenCalledWith(\n        '/state_sync',\n        expect.objectContaining({\n          autoConnect: false,\n          transports: ['polling', 'websocket'],\n          withCredentials: true,\n        })\n      );\n    });\n\n    it('should return same socket on subsequent calls', () => {\n      const socket1 = initStateSyncSocket();\n      const socket2 = initStateSyncSocket();\n\n      expect(socket1).toBe(socket2);\n      expect(io).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1);\n    });\n\n    it('should setup auth callback', () => {\n      initStateSyncSocket();\n\n      const config = (io as jest.Mock).mock.calls[0][1];\n      expect(config.auth).toBeInstanceOf(Function);\n    });\n\n    it('should fetch CSRF token in auth callback', async () => {\n      initStateSyncSocket();\n\n      const config = (io as jest.Mock).mock.calls[0][1];\n      const mockCb = jest.fn();\n\n      await config.auth(mockCb);\n\n      expect(csrfModule.getCsrfToken).toHaveBeenCalled();\n      expect(mockCb).toHaveBeenCalledWith({ csrf_token: 'test-token' });\n    });\n\n    it('should handle CSRF token failure in auth callback', async () => {\n      (csrfModule.getCsrfToken as jest.Mock).mockRejectedValue(new Error('CSRF error'));\n      const consoleSpy = jest.spyOn(console, 'error').mockImplementation();\n\n      initStateSyncSocket();\n\n      const config = (io as jest.Mock).mock.calls[0][1];\n      const mockCb = jest.fn();\n\n      await config.auth(mockCb);\n\n      expect(consoleSpy).toHaveBeenCalledWith(\n        expect.stringContaining('CSRF token fetch failed'),\n        expect.any(Error)\n      );\n      expect(mockCb).toHaveBeenCalledWith({});\n\n      consoleSpy.mockRestore();\n    });\n\n    it('should clear CSRF token on connect_error', () => {\n      initStateSyncSocket();\n\n      expect(mockSocket.on).toHaveBeenCalledWith('connect_error', expect.any(Function));\n\n      const errorHandler = mockSocket.on.mock.calls.find(\n        ([event]: [string]) => event === 'connect_error'\n      )[1];\n\n      errorHandler();\n\n      expect(csrfModule.clearCsrfToken).toHaveBeenCalled();\n    });\n\n    it('should use custom URL from env var', () => {\n      process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_A0_URL = 'http://custom:5000';\n\n      initStateSyncSocket();\n\n      expect(io).toHaveBeenCalledWith(\n        'http://custom:5000/state_sync',\n        expect.any(Object)\n      );\n\n      delete process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_A0_URL;\n    });\n  });\n\n  describe('getStateSyncSocket', () => {\n    it('should return null initially', () => {\n      expect(getStateSyncSocket()).toBeNull();\n    });\n\n    it('should return socket after init', () => {\n      initStateSyncSocket();\n\n      expect(getStateSyncSocket()).toBe(mockSocket);\n    });\n  });\n\n  describe('disconnectAll', () => {\n    it('should disconnect socket', () => {\n      initStateSyncSocket();\n\n      disconnectAll();\n\n      expect(mockSocket.disconnect).toHaveBeenCalled();\n      expect(getStateSyncSocket()).toBeNull();\n    });\n\n    it('should handle disconnect when no socket exists', () => {\n      expect(() => disconnectAll()).not.toThrow();\n    });\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## 10. `src/lib/utils.ts`\n\n### Untested Functions\n- ✗ `cn` utility\n\n### Test Skeletons\n\n```typescript\n// __tests__/lib/utils.test.ts\nimport { cn } from '@/lib/utils';\n\ndescribe('utils', () => {\n  describe('cn', () => {\n    it('should combine class names', () => {\n      expect(cn('foo', 'bar')).toBe('foo bar');\n    });\n\n    it('should handle conditional classes with clsx', () => {\n      expect(cn('foo', false && 'bar', 'baz')).toBe('foo baz');\n    });\n\n    it('should merge Tailwind classes', () => {\n      expect(cn('px-2 py-1', 'px-4')).toBe('py-1 px-4'); // tailwind-merge dedupes\n    });\n\n    it('should handle empty inputs', () => {\n      expect(cn()).toBe('');\n    });\n\n    it('should handle null and undefined', () => {\n      expect(cn('foo', null, undefined, 'bar')).toBe('foo bar');\n    });\n\n    it('should handle arrays', () => {\n      expect(cn(['foo', 'bar'], 'baz')).toBe('foo bar baz');\n    });\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## Summary of Major Gaps\n\n### Critical Missing Tests\n1. **Error handling** - Almost no error boundary tests across all hooks\n2. **Race conditions** - Concurrent operations, rapid state changes\n3. **WebSocket integration** - Socket reconnection, authentication flows\n4. **Type safety** - Malformed data from APIs/sockets\n5. **Memory leaks** - Timer cleanup, ref management, event listener removal\n6. **Edge cases** - Null/undefined values, empty arrays, missing fields\n\n### Recommended Next Steps\n1. Start with **use-socket.ts** and **csrf.ts** (critical infrastructure)\n2. Add integration tests for **use-chat.ts** + WebSocket flow\n3. Test error recovery paths in all data-fetching hooks\n4. Add E2E tests for complete user workflows (chat → action cards)\n5. Set up test coverage reporting to track progress\n",
